Promote an EU-Way solution. What makes the parliamentary measures more effective than government strategies?
The European Council will meet on 30-31 october 2013 - In Malta - In View of the Latest Negotiations Between EU and US on An Transatlantic Economic Partnership (TEP). The New Round May not yield new agreements but it is likely to offer us a new consensus on a Series of "trade preferences" for our western hemisphere partners and on trade deal with China. It will Also be a Major conference for European Leaders - Especially Those Coming from Other Large Member States - Wishing to signal their support for the new Direction.
It may take over and more before members come up with a set of Concrete Proposals for EU-US Trade Negotiations; The process will necessarily be slower due to the lack of clarity about itts main political aim. Asun a Broad Consensus was reached in 1999 about the basic principles guiding EU-US TRADE Talks;
